  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Statistical Regional Cooperation Western Balkans 2019-2023 - Statistical regional cooperation Western Balkans 2019-2023, ny strategi</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Statistiskt regionalt samarbete V&#xe4;stra Balkan 2019-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Statistics Sweden (SCB) have applied for a total of 19 122 000 SEK in order to implement &quot;Regional Cooperation Project in South Eastern Europe&quot; (Albania, Bosnien &amp; Herzegovina, Kosovo, Macedonia, Montenegro och Serbia) during 2019-2023. This is the fourth and final phase in the cooperation between SCB and the respective national statistical institutes.

The development objective of this fourth project phase are well developed stastitical systems in the region in line with the EU acquis for stastics. The project objective is that the National Statistical Institutes (NSIs) of the region actively engage each other regarding support and transfer of know-how with reference to more efficient statistical production and adaptation ot EU standards and acquis.

The component objectives are:

1) The NSIs are able to produce statistics more efficiently by using administrative date, with retained or improved quality
2) The NSIs are jointly able to supply each other with training and support, consistent with EU standards and EU acquis.
3) The Summer School institutionalised and fully owned by the NSIs in the region.

By contributing to the strengthening and institutionalisation of the cooperation between the national statistic authorities in the region the capacity building provided in previous project phases is expected to be strengthened and as such contributes to the long term sustainability of good standards for respective countries statistics.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Statistiska Centralbyr&#xe5;n (SCB) har s&#xf6;kt om medel om totalt 19 122 000 SEK f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra &quot;Regional Cooperation Project in South Eastern Europe&quot;  (Albanien, Bosnien &amp; Herzegovina, Kosovo, Macedonien, Montenegro och Serbien) under perioden 2019-2023. Denna insats omfattar en fj&#xe4;rde och sista fas i samarbetet.

Syftet med insatsen &#xe4;r  att utveckla statistiska system i regionen i linje med EUs acquis f&#xf6;r statistik. Insatsens syftar till att de nationella statistikmyndigheterna i respektive samarbetsland i regionen aktivt engagerar och st&#xf6;djer varandra samt bidrar till gemensam kapacitetsutveckling, delar med sig av varandras kunskap och erfarenheter om att utveckla statistik och anpassning till EUs standards och acquis.

I insatsens komponenter ing&#xe5;r:
1) Att de nationella statistik myndigheterna producerar statistik mer effektivt genom att anv&#xe4;nda administrativ data, med bibeh&#xe5;llen och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad kvalite;
2) Att de nationella statistik myndigheterna gemensamt bidrar till utbildningar och st&#xf6;d till varandra, i enlighet med EUs standards och EUs acquis;
3) Att sommarskolorna institutionaliseras och fullt ut &#xe4;gs av de nationella statistik myndigheterna i regionen.

Genom att bidra till att st&#xe4;rka och institutionalisera samarbetet mellan de nationella statistik myndigheterna i regionen v&#xe4;ntas den kapacitetsutvecklingen som ing&#xe5;tt i tidigare faser st&#xe4;rkas och skapa b&#xe4;ttre f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningar f&#xf6;r l&#xe5;ngsiktig h&#xe5;llbarhet vad g&#xe4;ller god standard f&#xf6;r respektive lands statistik.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project includes the following component objectives:
1. The national statistical institutes are able to produce statistics more efficiently by using administrative data, with retained or improved quality.
2. The national statistical institutes are jointly able to supply each other with training and support, consistent with EU standards and EU acquis.
3. The Summer School institutionalised and fully owned by the national statistical institutes in the region.
The project will include administrative data and registers; survery methodology; and summer schools.</narrative>
  </description>
